{"expected_head":"1cc4dd40e761e5c578c1e1ee594be283795e66a8","expected_base":"f9197185b624a8c3f74c99e48a69550b5a7c2a73","current_base":"f9197185b624a8c3f74c99e48a69550b5a7c2a73","pr":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thanhtuyen662002/Medcom/pulls/44","id":4708236117,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUygoWs8AAAABGKH7VQ","html_url":"https://github.com/thanhtuyen662002/Medcom/pull/44","diff_url":"https://github.com/thanhtuyen662002/Medcom/pull/44.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/thanhtuyen662002/Medcom/pull/44.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thanhtuyen662002/Medcom/issues/44","number":44,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Integrate ERP authentication, scoped document UI and verified full SQL source","user":{"login":"thanhtuyen662002","id":132963766,"node_id":"U_kgDOB-zdtg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132963766?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thanhtuyen662002","html_url":"https://github.com/thanhtuyen662002","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thanhtuyen662002/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thanhtuyen662002/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thanhtuyen662002/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thanhtuyen662002/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thanhtuyen662002/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thanhtuyen662002/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thanhtuyen662002/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thanhtuyen662002/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thanhtuyen662002/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Medcom integrates the pinned owner Tools.dll normal stored-password path, server-authoritative SQL identity/sessions and scoped purchase-order/inbound-request lists and line details in BE/FE. Password/system fallback shortcuts, generic CRUD and unverified business writes are excluded. Typed read queries check enabled current grants and frozen/current branch scope at SQL execution; quantities retain exact decimal precision. FE supports keyboard details, focus restoration and contained mobile tables.\n\nThe owner identified that procedure/trigger definitions were already in the supplied ZIP. Integrity verification found the prior extracted SQL was truncated: 1,015,021,568 bytes versus the member's 1,212,595,716 bytes. The complete member now matches ZIP size/CRC and SHA-256 61a8744c7a9a007b13ef37fbda26ea8c78af11fcc469963a528eba9469174096. Previous zero-procedure/absence conclusions are withdrawn.\n\nThe corrected finite catalog covers 596 tables, 211 views, 109 functions, 609 procedures and two sequences: 1,527 declared objects/33 checksummed members, with all headers reconciled. All seven transfer edit/delete checks are present among 28 transfer procedures. A separate stored-definition catalog preserves 188 declarations/160 unique module names, including six trigger records/three trigger names and their version provenance; stored definitions are distinct from outer DDL/current deployment.\n\nArchive tooling verifies full decompression, member size, CRC and hash before atomic replacement. Catalog/CI checks bind source size/hash to the finite manifest. Metadata exports contain no SQL bodies, raw data, owner binaries, credentials or unrelated row values.\n\nValidation on `692a8ab05ab248dbaad58a65f4c18893fbe34ca5`:\n- 37 source-free backend tests pass; source analyzer/build passes.\n- Three private runtime tests pass with actual owner DLL/source DDL and synthetic rows in disposable SQL Server. The new test executes the seven actual transfer checks plus their delegated helper on three source transfer tables. It verifies owner/PM/technician assignments, accepted/rejected status boundaries, missing IDs, linked-request deletion denial, source null-PM behavior and role status-list delegation.\n- Existing actual HTTPS browser coverage verifies normal SQL/DLL login, both document detail shapes, exact quantities, keyboard/mobile behavior, scope denial and logout/replay. Five FE contracts and four packaged browser checks remain separate from private runtime tests.\n- Nine archive/scanner/binding regressions and full catalog validation pass locally. Public CI excludes private owner-artifact runtime tests.\n- Hosted source-correction-head CI (historical after workflow commits): [run 37029121428](https://github.com/thanhtuyen662002/Medcom/actions/runs/37029121428) passed every step, including analyzer/backend tests, reference checks, full catalog/nine regressions, FE contracts/types/build, packaging and HTTPS browser checks.\n\nThe missing-procedure source blocker is **resolved**. Full business commands/effects, trusted action/branch checks, atomic writes/idempotency/concurrency, durable audit, legacy host/trigger version reconciliation, reporting/export, operations/performance and independent review/deployed-host acceptance remain open. Source checks do not replace Web authorization; source request keys are nvarchar(50), but check parameters are varchar(30), so command work must prevent truncation/encoding loss. No Web mutation or production deployment is enabled by the source tests. Candidate readiness remains 503 with BLOCKED_BUSINESS_AND_RUNTIME_ACCEPTANCE. Six distinct hourly production tasks are enabled under goal #45: five scoped coders staggered by ten minutes and one lead/integrator. Four historical Medcom tasks remain paused. Their create-only claims and invocation-owned work branches preserve serial integration; full dispatcher credential fencing remains unproved.\n\nEvidence: docs/erp/OWNER_SOURCE_RECOVERY_20261002.md, inventories/source/20261002/extraction-integrity.json, manifest.json, embedded-module-catalog.json, recovered-transfer-checks.json and runtime-receipt.json. Refs #12, #14, #19, #21, #28, #31, #33, #35, #42.\n\nProduction goal/workflow added in `ff835e444faa1587d1df00dc98c2cc4b6ce8dcb1`; observed six-task activation registry in `a78e71f0852fab1edb8daf161cd49ffb1481ed04`. See docs/goals/PRODUCTION_ERP_GOAL.md and docs/execution/PRODUCTION_WORKFLOW_20261002.md/production-tickets.json/production-schedules.json. This activates coding toward production; it does not claim product or target-host acceptance. Recheck CI on the latest live head.\n\nCurrent-round owner source recovery locators are now durable in source-set/SOURCE_BASELINE, commit `1cc4dd40e761e5c578c1e1ee594be283795e66a8`; scheduled sessions need not rely on transient private workspace paths. Interactive code publication is complete; scheduled lead owns subsequent integration. Current workflow-head CI is pending until actual checks complete.","created_at":"2026-10-01T19:00:24Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T16:32:51Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"416e32c143134012a38ec37de337e883376e31ba","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thanhtuyen662002/Medcom/pulls/44/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thanhtuyen662002/Medcom/pulls/44/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thanhtuyen662002/Medcom/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thanhtuyen662002/Medcom/issues/44/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thanhtuyen662002/Medcom/statuses/1cc4dd40e761e5c578c1e1ee594be283795e66a8","head":{"label":"thanhtuyen662002:medcom-schedule-activation-20261002","ref":"medcom-schedule-activation-20261002","sha":"1cc4dd40e761e5c578c1e1ee594be283795e66a8","user":{"login":"thanhtuyen662002","id":132963766,"node_id":"U_kgDOB-zdtg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132963766?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thanhtuyen662002","html_url":"https://github.com/thanhtuyen662002","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thanht